In fact, I forgot to mention that speed is a fifth desirable and that 
gauntlets of swimming are not the best way to avoid being drowned in a 
pool (your stuff will get wet).  To have all five desirables permanently 
is difficult for most classes.  Drain resistance and reflection take up 
the armor and amulet slots, unless you use the shield of reflection 
which is not a serious option for spellcasters.  But then the only good 
way to avoid pools is to wear water walking boots, so you don't have 
permanent speed.  (You can use potions or the haste self spell. Of 
course, if you keep your bag of holding in an oilskin sack and have 
rustproofed all your stuff, you might as well take speed boots and 
gauntlets of swimming.  Which does not help against falling into the 
castle moat.)  Also, the fact that magic resistance as not provided by 
an artifact is then essentially obtainable only by wearing the cloak may 
mean that you have to exchange your early gray dragon scale mail later...
